    "body": "## Summary\n\n`examples/coding_agent_rl/swe.py::_repository_tree` excludes the harness metadata directory with a pathspec:\n\n```\ngit add -A -- . ':(exclude)PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md' ':(exclude).harness/'\n```\n\nWhen the task repo's own `.gitignore` already ignores `.harness` (for example a `.*` rule), `git add` treats the pathspec as naming an ignored path and exits 1:\n\n```\nThe following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files:\n.harness\nhint: Use -f if you really want to add them.\n```\n\n`sb.exec(..., check=True)` then raises, `git_diff` fails, and `generate` aborts the rollout (`exception:RuntimeError`) before grading. Every rollout on such a repo is lost, regardless of the model.\n\nThis PR keeps `.harness/` out of the snapshot through a temporary `core.excludesFile` instead of a pathspec.\n\n## How we hit it\n\nRunning MiMo-V2.6-RL-oss `format-code-task-002561` (sfcc-ci) with the Claude Code harness, all 4 rollouts aborted. The image ships sfcc-ci's upstream `.gitignore`, which contains `.*` / `!.github` (unchanged since 2019 in SalesforceCommerceCloud/sfcc-ci). On a fresh sandbox, calling `swe._repository_tree` directly:\n\n| state | result |\n| --- | --- |\n| repo as shipped, no `.harness/` | ok |\n| after the harness creates `.harness/` (as `slime/agent/harness/common.py` always does) | fails with the error above |\n| `.harness/` present, `.*` removed from `.gitignore` | ok |\n\nReproduced with git 2.39.5 (in the image) and git 2.50.1.\n\n## Fix\n\n```sh\nharness_excludes=$(mktemp)    # removed by the existing EXIT trap\necho .harness/ > \"$harness_excludes\"\ngit -c core.excludesFile=\"$harness_excludes\" add -A -- . ':(exclude)PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md'\n```\n\nThe snapshot content is unchanged:\n\n- `.harness/` stays out whether or not the repo ignores it;\n- the repo's own ignore rules still apply;\n- `PROBLEM_STATEMENT.md` is still excluded by pathspec (it is not ignored, so that pathspec is safe).\n\nSimply dropping `':(exclude).harness/'` would not be correct: on repos that do not ignore dot directories, `.harness/` would then end up in the patch.\n\n`git_diff`'s `git diff ... ':(exclude).harness/'` is left as is: `git diff` between two trees does not reject pathspecs that match ignored paths.\n\n## Test\n\nAdds `test_patch_when_repo_gitignore_ignores_dot_directories` to `tests/test_agent/test_swe_workspace_diff.py` (already part of the CPU `agent-test` CI job). It uses the existing `LocalShell` / real git setup.\n\n- Without the fix: the new test fails with the error above; the 3 existing tests pass.\n- With the fix: 4 passed.\n- `pre-commit run` on the changed files: all hooks pass.\n",
